    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d62">

                <pb facs="0098" n="88" sameAs="frus:frus1944v02/pg88"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">840.50/9–2944: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Winant</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-09-29T17:00:00+01:00">September 29,
                            1944—5 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received September 29—4 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>8139. In trying to collect information you wanted in Department’s 7647, September
                    19, I would suggest that you talk with Law and Penrose if, on leaving the UNRRA
                    Council meeting in Montreal,<anchor n="97" xml:id="d62-f1"/> they are returning
                    to London through Washington.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Winant</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d62-f1" n="97" xml:id="d62-f1-content">
                <p>With regard to the second session of the United Nations Relief and Rehabilitation
                    Administration’s Council at Montreal, September 1944, see <ref target="#pg334"
                        >pp. 334</ref> and <ref target="#pg338">338</ref>–<ref target="#pg354"
                        >354</ref>, <hi rendition="#italic">passim;</hi> for documentation relating
                    to the establishment of UNRRA, see <ref target="frus1943v01#pg_851">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Foreign Relations</hi>, 1943, vol. <hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">i</hi>, pp. 851</ref> ff.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
